The fox tilted its head. “That’s not a reason. That’s an excuse.”

Barnaby blinked. “What do you mean?”

“Cats don’t chase things because they want to catch them,” the fox said. “They chase things because they want to find something else.”

Barnaby considered this. He had never thought about chasing as anything more than chasing. But now, as he looked around the strange forest, he wondered if he was searching for something he couldn’t name.

The butterfly fluttered onward.

